the bracket starts with the mark on the bytes already live, not on zero: true
the workload ran and produced its output: true
running the workload raises the mark by at least the bytes it computes into: true
the mark is never below what is live under it: true
releasing the context gives the bytes back, so the live gauge falls: true
and the mark stays where the workload put it: true
so a reading taken after the window would understate it by the bytes just freed: true
a rebase puts the mark back on the live bytes: true
so the window that follows does not inherit the earlier peak: true
the mark takes in every pool live at once, not the largest one: true
a free lowers the live bytes: true
and leaves the mark untouched: true
growing a pool in place adds its growth, not its whole new size: true
the mark rises only where the growth passes the earlier high water: true
a bigger total does raise the mark: true
the fabricated pools are all given back: true
a rebase after them lands on the live bytes, not on the high water: true
